# w69-flashback (the operator, 2026-10-11, on Cabal Therapy): "it was awkward to play from the graveyard.
# i was like dragging an arrow from the graveyard, but it should be possible to pick up cards from the
# graveyard if they have flashback. so i should be able to drag them and play them like a spell, not have
# a target arrow drawn. the target arrow should come after the spell is played." Alice's graveyard is
# Island, Think Twice, Firebolt (Firebolt on top, drawn whole). Five Mountains and three Islands pay both
# flashbacks ({4}{R}, then {2}{U}), so Forge offers both from the graveyard at her main phase; Firebolt
# asks its target only once cast. The Island under them is a card the pile opens from (a click on an
# offered card is that card's own). The Island in hand keeps the main phase a real stop.
turn=1
